==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|tutour}} {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|tutour}}, from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|tuteur}} (French {{term|tuteur}}), from {{etyl|la}} {{term|tutor|lang=la||a watcher, protector, guardian}}, from {{term|tueri|tuēri|to protect}}; see [[tuition]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-tutor.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|uːtə(r)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[teaches]] another (usually called a ''[[student]]'', ''[[learner]]'', or ''[[tutee]]'') in a one-on-one or small-group interaction.
#: ''He passed the difficult class with help from his '''tutor'''.''

